  "worldbuilding_rules": [
    "Keep the existing game systems and interaction model unless a Gambian replacement requires a gameplay change.",
    "Prefer real Gambian anchors for named places and use fictional names only when there is no sensible one-to-one real venue.",
    "Do not imply that Banjul, Serrekunda, Kololi and Senegambia are interchangeable. They should feel different in the game.",
    "Keep Serrekunda as the affordable everyday/commercial heart.",
    "Keep Senegambia/Kololi as the nightlife and tourism-heavy social zone.",
    "Keep Banjul as the compact capital/government zone.",
    "Use Bakau/Fajara for sports, older coastal neighbourhoods and middle-to-upper-end leisure.",
    "Use Sukuta, Bijilo, Brufut and Brikama for expansion and more residential/regional gameplay.",
    "Use Gambian food and transport terms in missions, NPC dialogue, ads and random events rather than only changing place labels.",
    "Avoid copying real brand identities too closely when a fictional in-game business can do the job; real landmarks and public institutions are preferred as anchors."
  ]
}
